      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The activity of potassium, sodium, magnesium and Ca-ATP-ase of the erythrocytic membrane, index of erythrocyte deformability, changes of the hemodynamics and some cardiac function during bicycle ergometry [correction of veloergometry] tests before and after a course of laser irradiation of the blood were studied in 36 patients with exertion stenocardia. It was established that laser therapy is accompanied by increase of the activity of ATP-ase, index of erythrocyte deformability and positive changes of the cardial function. The possibility is discussed of improving the cardiac function under the effect of laser irradiation as a result of optimization of the structural-functional organization of the cellular membrane."},
